# DSA Revision Agent — Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This is an AI-powered DSA revision agent built as a capstone project
for the Agentic AI Engineering & Systems Automation Fellowship.

## Architecture
- Backend: Python + FastAPI
- AI Layer: Claude API (Anthropic)
- Database: Supabase
- Frontend: Plain HTML/CSS/JS
- Deployment: Railway

## Coding Rules
- Never hardcode API keys or secrets. Always use environment variables.
- All AI calls must use the DSA Analyzer persona defined in prompts/dsa_analyzer.md
- Every function must have a docstring explaining what it does.
- Validate all incoming webhook payloads before processing.
- Return structured JSON from all AI calls — never freeform text.
- Log errors properly — never silently swallow exceptions.

## File Structure
- backend/ — FastAPI server, webhook handler, AI layer, database layer
- frontend/ — Dashboard (HTML/CSS/JS)
- prompts/ — All system prompts and persona definitions
- .env.example — Documents all required environment variables
- README.md — Architecture, setup, usage